# Build context for the image built by ./Dockerfile.
#
# The image installs a wheel built from this tree, so the context needs the
# packaged sources and nothing else. Two entries are load-bearing rather than
# cosmetic:
#
#   .env        — a real, git-ignored credential file. `git` never sees it, so
#                 nothing else in this repository stops it from being copied
#                 into a layer and shipped inside a published image.
#   .venv       — a host virtualenv carries absolute paths and host-arch
#                 binaries. Copied in, it shadows nothing but costs hundreds of
#                 megabytes and invalidates the layer cache on every local run.
#
# The rest is size and cache hygiene: readme-gifs-hd/ alone is ~89 MB, tests/
# ~18 MB, and neither is installed.

# secrets and local configuration
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# version control and host environments
.git
.gitignore
.venv
venv
node_modules

# caches and build outputs
#
# `**/` on everything that nests. A pattern without a separator is matched
# against the whole path relative to the context root, so a bare `__pycache__`
# excludes only one at the top level — and there isn't one — while the 6 MB
# spread through openai4s/, skills/ and scripts/ rides along and busies the
# layer cache on every stray .pyc.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
dist
build
.build
**/*.isorted

# not installed by the wheel
readme-gifs-hd
assets
tests
harness
epibench_eval
.github
docs/*.png

# macOS
**/.DS_Store
